{
  "schema": 2,
  "generated": "2026-10-10",
  "purpose": "Ties each firmware image to the processing .cfg that correctly labels its range and Doppler axes. Processing MUST refuse to run if the --cfg passed does not match the flashed image recorded in ~/.radar_flashed. A mismatch reports ranges wrong by up to 10.0x (r168m cfg on r017m data) and Doppler wrong by up to 4.7x, with no other symptom. r017m and r017m_calib share a slope, so the slope alone cannot tell them apart -- idle_time_us is what distinguishes them.",
  "conventions": {
    "hashes": "lowercase hex, md5. Compare case-insensitively; PowerShell Get-FileHash emits uppercase.",
    "registers": "The *_reg / *_us / *_ghz fields are transcribed from cascade_config.h and are the source of truth. Every derived field below them is recomputed from these, so the map proves itself.",
    "derived": "slope_mhz_us = freq_slope_const x 0.0482797623 (TI LSB = 3.6e6 x 900 / 2^26 kHz/us; NOT 48 kHz/us). max_range_m = c.fs/(2.slope); range_res_m = max_range_m/num_adc_samples; hpf_floor_m = f_hpf2 x c/(2.slope); v_max_mps = lambda/(4.num_chirps.(idle+ramp)); v_res_mps = v_max_mps/(num_loops/2). c = 299792458. hpf1_floor_m = f_hpf1 x c/(2.slope). fps = 1000/frame_periodicity_ms. frame_bytes = num_adc_samples x num_chirps x num_loops x 8 RX x 4 B.",
    "identities": "max_range_m == range_res_m x num_adc_samples, and v_max_mps/v_res_mps == num_loops/2. Both are forced by the FFT sizes and hold for every variant; a violation means a value was hand-edited.",
    "hpf_registers": "HPF1 reg 0/1/2/3 = 175/235/350/700 kHz; HPF2 reg 0/1/2/3/4/5/6/7 = 0.35/0.7/1.4/2.8/5/7.5/10/15 MHz (rl_sensor.h / common.c CHIRP_HPF*_CORNER_FREQ_*). Before 2026-10-10 hpf1_floor_m was computed with 700 kHz for reg 2 and was 2x too large; corrected for every variant.",
    "compression": "The cascade firmware never configures compression (no compression call in common.c / main_mss.c / mmwave control). 'off' for every image. The 'compressionCfg ... 1 ...' line in older .cfg files was inert and wrong.",
    "dss_l3_meminit": "true = image runs SOC_rcmStartMemInitDSSL3 at boot (main_mss.c). Images with false stream ~50% stale words per chirp when booted from QSPI; see investigation/REPORT.md.",
    "iq_order": "Every image: int16 little-endian, I then Q (rlDevDataFmtCfg iqSwapSel=0, main_mss.c). adcbufCfg SampleSwap must be 0 in every processing .cfg.",
    "dca_wire_time": "The frame's time on the wire at the DCA1000 packet delay must be shorter than frame_periodicity_ms, or the DCA streams back-to-back and drops LVDS data internally (invisible to sequence-number and byte-count checks). CONFIG_PACKET_DATA delay is in 8 ns ticks; each packet takes ~delay + 12.2 us; frame_bytes/1456 = 2160.5 packets. 50 us (6250): 134.4 ms per frame -> max 7.44 fps. 25 us (3125): ~80 ms per frame -> 8 fps OK. Use 25 us for every 8 fps image.",
    "v2_family": "*_v2 images (2026-10-10): the base variant's cascade_config.h block unchanged except HPF1/HPF2 = 0/0 (175/350 kHz) and, for *_8fps, frame_periodicity_ms = 125. All carry the DSS L3 MEMINIT fix. r017m_calib_v2 keeps 1000 ms. Each image disassembly-diffed against its base image: only MEMINIT, the HPF store and the frame-period immediate differ.",
    "antenna_calibration": "antennaCalibParams are inherited unchanged from the original shortrange .cfg (77 GHz set: r017m*) and longrange .cfg (76 GHz set: every other variant). Their provenance and the HPF they were measured with are not recorded; the 76 GHz set came from a profile with HPF 2/2. Repeat the calibration with the HPF 0/0 images before trusting angle estimates: r017m_calib_v2 for 77 GHz, a 76 GHz v2 image for the 76 GHz variants."
  },
  "hash_notes": {
    "xer5f": "NEVER use. Non-deterministic: 3-4 distinct images per variant from identical source (86.7% metadata). Not recorded here for that reason.",
    "rprc": "Deterministic. Fingerprint of compiled parameters; verifies a rebuild.",
    "appimage": "Deterministic. Identifies the artefact written to QSPI at 0xA0000."
  },
